  "title": "First Fleet arrival at Sydney Cove",
  "summary": "Eleven ships under Captain Arthur Phillip left Portsmouth on 13 May 1787 carrying 759 convicts. After calls at Tenerife, Rio de Janeiro and Cape Town they entered Botany Bay in January 1788, then anchored in Sydney Cove on 26 January, beginning the British settlement of New South Wales on Gadigal Country.",
